<tr><td><b>Campaign total</b></td><td></td><td><b>2,044</b></td><td><b>8.46%</b></td><td><b>2,088.24</b></td><td></td></tr></table>
<p class="mut">One keyword drove about 74% of the week's spend. Impression share was 67.5% in this week.</p></div>
</section>

<section id="t-evidence" class="tab">
<div class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Reality check</div><h2>What the data does not show yet</h2>
<ul class="x">
<li><b>No verified leads.</b> September's single conversion was my test. One conversion appeared on 1 to 7 Oct on a "restaurant interior design" keyword and still needs confirming as a real enquiry.</li>
<li><b>Budget was the limit.</b> At AED 83 a day the campaign was budget-limited. After the raise, clicks per day went from 7.2 (3 to 30 Sep average) to 24.7 at a similar CPC. I first read this as a keyword volume problem, and I was wrong.</li>
<li><b>The <code>{ignore}</code> URL template</b> still appears in landing page reports through 30 Sep, while users reached clean URLs. I treat it as housekeeping, not a proven cause.</li>
<li><b>Small samples.</b> Each phase is 60 to 170 clicks, so differences between phases can be noise.</li></ul></div>
